From bb3df889e1a135ee9b4bb66bde0754c2e7f5737e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 05:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(catalogues): the documents enter the agentic graph, and
 CI can read them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two gaps, found by running the guards against the merged tree rather than by
reading the diff.

CI COULD NOT HAVE READ THE PDFs

verify-business-facts.mjs reads the text of every PDF served from public/ and
looks for retired claims — a price band that changed, a figure withdrawn. It
fails rather than skips when pdftotext is absent, which is correct and is why
F-23 is in its header. Eleven catalogues are now published, so eleven documents a
customer downloads and keeps are inside that check — and the Guards job installs
nothing but Node. It would have failed on the first run, or worse, passed on a
runner image that happened to carry poppler-utils and failed silently the day
that changed. The job installs it explicitly now.

THE DOCUMENTS WERE IN EVERY TEXT SURFACE AND NONE OF THE MACHINE ONES

/catalogues, the rails, /resources, /technical-library, the sitemap, llms.txt,
llms-full.txt, ai.txt and /api/knowledge all carried them. lib/registry — the
/api/v1 primitives, the OpenAPI document, the entity graph — carried nothing:
`grep -c catalogue` returned 0 for both registry.ts and manifest.ts. So an agent
working from the versioned API could not discover that eleven documents exist.

/api/v1/catalogues closes it, and the field that earns the endpoint is `related`.
An assistant asked "have you got anything on refinishing versus replacing"
should be able to hand over the document AND the page that argues it at length,
and this is the only surface that states which page goes with which document.
Each entry is gated on the file existing, and the payload states its refusals the
way the other endpoints do.

scripts/verify-catalogues.mjs holds the whole arrangement: every listed document
is a file on disk, every file on disk is listed (an unlisted PDF is served but
unfindable — and invisible to the fact check that reads it for retired claims),
filenames match their id because a filename here is a URL somebody has printed,
every related href and every rail route resolves, no price or percentage or
four-digit year is restated in prose, and neither the index page nor the API may
carry its own list instead of deriving one. Six regression tests, all six firing.

62 guards, 272 tests, tsc at the 115-error baseline, route parity now covering
116 URLs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018hun5TPKuy4M2JfTkF11NU
